+/// Upper bound on the number of line segments a single quadratic Bézier curve (a `QuadTo` path
+/// element) is flattened into.
+///
+/// Without this cap, the subdivision-count estimate (`params.val` in the `QuadTo` handling in
+/// [`flatten`]) grows with the affine transform's scale factor: at increasingly extreme "zoom"
+/// levels the estimate (and the resulting line count `n`) can reach into the billions, and the
+/// `for i in 1..n` loop that follows performs real, uncapped work with no allocation to fail and
+/// abort on - it just runs for as long as `n` demands, which for a sufficiently large transform
+/// scale is effectively forever (see <https://github.com/linebender/vello/issues/1752>). Clamping
+/// trades flattening accuracy for robustness in these edge cases; ordinary curves never come
+/// close to this limit. Mirrors `MAX_CUBIC_LINES`'s equivalent cap on the cubic (`CurveTo`) path
+/// in [`flatten_cubic_simd`].
+const MAX_QUAD_LINES: usize = 1 << 16;
